  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/aristotles-rhetoric> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Aristotle's fourth-century BCE treatise defining rhetoric as the ability to see the available means of persuasion in a given case; it introduced the three proofs of character, emotion and argument, and the first systematic analysis of how an audience shapes a speech." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/aristotles-rhetoric> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/scheme/thinkers-and-works> .
